<?xml version="1.0" encoding="ISO-8859-1"?>
<wps:ProcessDescriptions xmlns:wps="http://www.opengis.net/wps/1.0.0" xmlns:ows="http://www.opengis.net/ows/1.1" xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.opengis.net/wps/1.0.0 schemas/wps/1.0.0/wpsDescribeProcess_response.xsd" service="WPS" version="1.0.0" xml:lang="en-US">
	<ProcessDescription wps:processVersion="1" storeSupported="true" statusSupported="false">
		<ows:Identifier>MiraMon:Mosaic:1</ows:Identifier>
		<ows:Title>Option 1</ows:Title>
		<ows:Abstract>The region to Mosaic includes the whole region of all the SourceFiles indicated.</ows:Abstract>
		<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Title:Mosaic and join layers"/>
		<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Abstract:Given a set of layers that cover a determined region, for example a set of sheets of a certain cartographic cut, the program generates a resulting layer by combining the original layers."/>
		<DataInputs>
			<Input minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>Opcio</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Option</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>The region to Mosaic includes the whole region of all the SourceFiles indicated</ows:Abstract>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Param1"/>
				<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#integer">integer</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AllowedValues>
						<ows:Value>1</ows:Value>
					</ows:AllowedValues>
					<DefaultValue>1</DefaultValue>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>FitxersFont</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Source files</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>Is a list of files written one after another in a command line or a text file that contains the names of the preexisting files to use.</ows:Abstract>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Param3"/>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Name:SourceFiles"/>
				<ComplexData>
					<Default>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>text/plain</MimeType>
							<Encoding>ascii</Encoding>
						</Format>
					</Default>
					<Supported>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>text/plain</MimeType>
							<Encoding>ascii</Encoding>
						</Format>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>application/x-lst</MimeType>
							<Encoding>ascii</Encoding>
						</Format>
					</Supported>
				</ComplexData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>NODATA</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>NoData</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>Is the value used to fill in zones without data in any of the preexisting files; it has to be an integer (p.ex. 0). In the case that it is not indicated, the value of the first file on the list is used.</ows:Abstract>
				<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#double">double</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AnyValue/>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>TOLERANCIA</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Tolerance</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>Is the tolerance factor when adapting the coordinates of the cell matrices defined for each raster, to those of the first image.</ows:Abstract>
				<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#double">double</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AnyValue/>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>IMATGE_BUIDA</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Empty image</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract><![CDATA[What the program does if an empty image is generated (constant value or NoData) <ul><li>0: erase the image if all the values are equal or if they are NoData.</li><li>1: erase if the image has all the values as NoData or if it is completely outside the region.</li><li>2: generate an empty image even if it is entirely NoData or if it is outside the region.</li><li>if this parameter is not indicated images outside the region are not generated.</li></ul>]]></ows:Abstract>
				<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#integer">integer</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AllowedValues>
						<ows:Value>0</ows:Value>
						<ows:Value>1</ows:Value>
						<ows:Value>2</ows:Value>
					</ows:AllowedValues>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>VORA</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Limit</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>In the raster mosaics this indicates that it is necessary to ignore an 'n' cells wide border of each of the original images</ows:Abstract>
				<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#integer">integer</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AnyValue/>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>RLE</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Compress and index IMG</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>When the output file is an IMG file, this file will be compressed and indexed.</ows:Abstract>
				<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#string">string</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AllowedValues>
						<ows:Value>##blank##</ows:Value>
					</ows:AllowedValues>
					<DefaultValue>##blank##</DefaultValue>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>LLINATGE</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Lineage</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>Pattern for the name of an additional raster file (actually one for each band) that indicates the source file index (starting from 0) that has contributed to each pixel of the output image. This file can help you understand the source of the data in each pixel of the output image.</ows:Abstract>
				<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#string">string</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AnyValue/>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>SIMPLIFICA_VERTEXS</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Simplify the intermediate vertices</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>Simplify the intermediate vertices of the arcs, as long as this does not mean a change in topology.</ows:Abstract>
				<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#string">string</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AllowedValues>
						<ows:Value>##blank##</ows:Value>
					</ows:AllowedValues>
					<DefaultValue>##blank##</DefaultValue>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>ALGORISME</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Algorithm</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract><![CDATA[This parameter is used to determine the type of algorithm that the application will use to cut the vectors in the topological structure.<ul><li> ESCOMBRATGE Based on the intersection of segments Bentley-Ottmann. </li><li>DIRECTE: Based on the exploration of all segments against all segments to determine the intersections between Victor by the topological structure.</li><li>AUTOMATIC: MiraMon automatically decides which of the two algorithms used.</li></ul>]]></ows:Abstract>
				<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#string">string</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AllowedValues>
						<ows:Value>ESCOMBRATGE</ows:Value>
						<ows:Value>DIRECTE</ows:Value>
						<ows:Value>AUTOMATIC</ows:Value>
					</ows:AllowedValues>
					<DefaultValue>AUTOMATIC</DefaultValue>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>TITOL</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Title</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>Output file title</ows:Abstract>
				<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#string">string</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AnyValue/>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>PATRO_DEST</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Pattern for result files</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>Common pattern for result files in case of multiband files.</ows:Abstract>
				<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#string">string</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AnyValue/>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>
		</DataInputs>
		<ProcessOutputs>
			<Output>
				<ows:Identifier>FitxerDesti</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Destination file</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>Is the name of the file resulting from the mosaic.</ows:Abstract>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Param2"/>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Name:DestinationFile"/>
				<ComplexOutput>
					<Default>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>application/x-img</MimeType>
							<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
						</Format>
					</Default>
					<Supported>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>application/x-img</MimeType>
							<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
						</Format>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>image/jpeg</MimeType>
							<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
						</Format>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>application/x-pnt</MimeType>
							<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
						</Format>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>application/x-pol</MimeType>
							<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
						</Format>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>application/x-arc</MimeType>
							<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
						</Format>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>application/x-nod</MimeType>
							<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
						</Format>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>image/png</MimeType>
							<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
						</Format>
					</Supported>
				</ComplexOutput>
			</Output>
		</ProcessOutputs>
	</ProcessDescription>
	<ProcessDescription wps:processVersion="1" storeSupported="true" statusSupported="false">
		<ows:Identifier>MiraMon:Mosaic:2</ows:Identifier>
		<ows:Title>Option 2</ows:Title>
		<ows:Abstract>The region to Mosaic is indicated by the parameters Xminimum Xmaximum Yminimum Ymaximum.</ows:Abstract>
		<DataInputs>
			<Input minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>Opcio</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Option</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>The region to Mosaic is indicated by the parameters Xminimum Xmaximum Yminimum Ymaximum.</ows:Abstract>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Param1"/>
				<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#integer">integer</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AllowedValues>
						<ows:Value>2</ows:Value>
					</ows:AllowedValues>
					<DefaultValue>2</DefaultValue>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>Xmin</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>X minimum</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>X minimum coordinate of the output region. If these coordinates do not fit the pixel matrix defined by the first source image, they are adapted for excess.</ows:Abstract>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Param3"/>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Name:Xmin"/>
				<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#double">double</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AnyValue/>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>Xmax</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>X maximum</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>X maximum coordinate of the output region. If these coordinates do not fit the pixel matrix defined by the first source image, they are adapted for excess.</ows:Abstract>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Param4"/>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Name:Xmax"/>
				<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#double">double</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AnyValue/>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>Ymin</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Y minimum</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>Y minimum coordinate of the output region. If these coordinates do not fit the pixel matrix defined by the first source image, they are adapted for excess.</ows:Abstract>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Param5"/>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Name:Ymin"/>
				<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#double">double</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AnyValue/>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>Ymax</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Y maximum</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>Y maximum coordinate of the output region. If these coordinates do not fit the pixel matrix defined by the first source image, they are adapted for excess.</ows:Abstract>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Param6"/>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Name:Ymax"/>
				<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#double">double</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AnyValue/>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>FitxersFont</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Source files</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>Is a list of files written one after another in a command line or a text file that contains the names of the preexisting files to use.</ows:Abstract>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Param7"/>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Name:SourceFiles"/>
				<ComplexData>
					<Default>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>text/plain</MimeType>
							<Encoding>ascii</Encoding>
						</Format>
					</Default>
					<Supported>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>text/plain</MimeType>
							<Encoding>ascii</Encoding>
						</Format>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>application/x-lst</MimeType>
							<Encoding>ascii</Encoding>
						</Format>
					</Supported>
				</ComplexData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>NODATA</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>NoData</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>Is the value used to fill in zones without data in any of the preexisting files; it has to be an integer (p.ex. 0). In the case that it is not indicated, the value of the first file on the list is used.</ows:Abstract>
				<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#double">double</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AnyValue/>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>TOLERANCIA</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Tolerance</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>Is the tolerance factor when adapting the coordinates of the cell matrices defined for each raster, to those of the first image.</ows:Abstract>
				<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#double">double</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AnyValue/>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>IMATGE_BUIDA</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Empty image</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract><![CDATA[What the program does if an empty image is generated (constant value or NoData) <ul><li>0: erase the image if all the values are equal or if they are NoData.</li><li>1: erase if the image has all the values as NoData or if it is completely outside the region.</li><li>2: generate an empty image even if it is entirely NoData or if it is outside the region.</li><li>if this parameter is not indicated images outside the region are not generated.</li></ul>]]></ows:Abstract>
				<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#integer">integer</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AllowedValues>
						<ows:Value>0</ows:Value>
						<ows:Value>1</ows:Value>
						<ows:Value>2</ows:Value>
					</ows:AllowedValues>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>VORA</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Limit</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>In the raster mosaics this indicates that it is necessary to ignore an 'n' cells wide border of each of the original images</ows:Abstract>
				<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#integer">integer</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AnyValue/>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>RLE</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Compress and index IMG</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>When the output file is an IMG file, this file will be compressed and indexed.</ows:Abstract>
				<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#string">string</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AllowedValues>
						<ows:Value>##blank##</ows:Value>
					</ows:AllowedValues>
					<DefaultValue>##blank##</DefaultValue>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>LLINATGE</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Lineage</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>Pattern for the name of an additional raster file (actually one for each band) that indicates the source file index (starting from 0) that has contributed to each pixel of the output image. This file can help you understand the source of the data in each pixel of the output image.</ows:Abstract>
				<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#string">string</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AnyValue/>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>SIMPLIFICA_VERTEXS</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Simplify the intermediate vertices</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>Simplify the intermediate vertices of the arcs, as long as this does not mean a change in topology.</ows:Abstract>
				<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#string">string</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AllowedValues>
						<ows:Value>##blank##</ows:Value>
					</ows:AllowedValues>
					<DefaultValue>##blank##</DefaultValue>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>ALGORISME</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Algorithm</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract><![CDATA[This parameter is used to determine the type of algorithm that the application will use to cut the vectors in the topological structure.<ul><li> ESCOMBRATGE Based on the intersection of segments Bentley-Ottmann. </li><li>DIRECTE: Based on the exploration of all segments against all segments to determine the intersections between Victor by the topological structure.</li><li>AUTOMATIC: MiraMon automatically decides which of the two algorithms used.</li></ul>]]></ows:Abstract>
				<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#string">string</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AllowedValues>
						<ows:Value>ESCOMBRATGE</ows:Value>
						<ows:Value>DIRECTE</ows:Value>
						<ows:Value>AUTOMATIC</ows:Value>
					</ows:AllowedValues>
					<DefaultValue>AUTOMATIC</DefaultValue>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>TITOL</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Title</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>Output file title</ows:Abstract>
				<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#string">string</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AnyValue/>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>PATRO_DEST</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Pattern for result files</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>Common pattern for result files in case of multiband files.</ows:Abstract>
				<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#string">string</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AnyValue/>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>
		</DataInputs>
		<ProcessOutputs>
			<Output>
				<ows:Identifier>FitxerDesti</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Destination file</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>Is the name of the file resulting from the mosaic.</ows:Abstract>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Param2"/>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Name:DestinationFile"/>
				<ComplexOutput>
					<Default>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>application/x-img</MimeType>
							<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
						</Format>
					</Default>
					<Supported>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>application/x-img</MimeType>
							<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
						</Format>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>image/jpeg</MimeType>
							<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
						</Format>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>application/x-pnt</MimeType>
							<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
						</Format>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>application/x-pol</MimeType>
							<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
						</Format>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>application/x-arc</MimeType>
							<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
						</Format>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>application/x-nod</MimeType>
							<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
						</Format>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>image/png</MimeType>
							<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
						</Format>
					</Supported>
				</ComplexOutput>
			</Output>
		</ProcessOutputs>
	</ProcessDescription>
	<ProcessDescription wps:processVersion="1" storeSupported="true" statusSupported="false">
		<ows:Identifier>MiraMon:Mosaic:3</ows:Identifier>
		<ows:Title>Option 3</ows:Title>
		<ows:Abstract>The region to Mosaic is indicated by an irregular MaskFile (only for vectorial files). The objects outside the mask are eliminated.</ows:Abstract>
		<DataInputs>
			<Input minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>Opcio</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Option</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>The region to Mosaic is indicated by an irregular MaskFile (only for vectorial files). The objects outside the mask are eliminated.</ows:Abstract>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Param1"/>
				<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#integer">integer</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AllowedValues>
						<ows:Value>3</ows:Value>
					</ows:AllowedValues>
					<DefaultValue>3</DefaultValue>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>FitxerMascara</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Mask file</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract><![CDATA[is the name of a VEC file that defines an irregular polygon (only for vectors). In this case, there is the option to indicate a set of parameters that define the selection with the suffix "_MASCARA"  (p.ex: <i>/COND1_CAMP_MASCARA=</i>). To find out more about the values of these parameters there is more iformation in the document <a href="general.htm#SelecAtrib">general</a> syntax]]></ows:Abstract>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Param3"/>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Name:MaskFile"/>
				<ComplexData>
					<Default>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>application/x-pol</MimeType>
							<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
						</Format>
					</Default>
					<Supported>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>application/x-pol</MimeType>
							<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
						</Format>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>application/x-nod</MimeType>
							<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
						</Format>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>application/x-arc</MimeType>
							<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
						</Format>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>application/x-pnt</MimeType>
							<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
						</Format>
					</Supported>
				</ComplexData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>FitxersFont</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Source files</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>Is a list of files written one after another in a command line or a text file that contains the names of the preexisting files to use.</ows:Abstract>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Param4"/>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Name:SourceFiles"/>
				<ComplexData>
					<Default>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>text/plain</MimeType>
							<Encoding>ascii</Encoding>
						</Format>
					</Default>
					<Supported>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>text/plain</MimeType>
							<Encoding>ascii</Encoding>
						</Format>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>application/x-lst</MimeType>
							<Encoding>ascii</Encoding>
						</Format>
					</Supported>
				</ComplexData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>NODATA</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>NoData</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>Is the value used to fill in zones without data in any of the preexisting files; it has to be an integer (p.ex. 0). In the case that it is not indicated, the value of the first file on the list is used.</ows:Abstract>
				<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#double">double</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AnyValue/>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>TOLERANCIA</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Tolerance</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>Is the tolerance factor when adapting the coordinates of the cell matrices defined for each raster, to those of the first image.</ows:Abstract>
				<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#double">double</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AnyValue/>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>IMATGE_BUIDA</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Empty image</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract><![CDATA[What the program does if an empty image is generated (constant value or NoData) <ul><li>0: erase the image if all the values are equal or if they are NoData.</li><li>1: erase if the image has all the values as NoData or if it is completely outside the region.</li><li>2: generate an empty image even if it is entirely NoData or if it is outside the region.</li><li>if this parameter is not indicated images outside the region are not generated.</li></ul>]]></ows:Abstract>
				<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#integer">integer</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AllowedValues>
						<ows:Value>0</ows:Value>
						<ows:Value>1</ows:Value>
						<ows:Value>2</ows:Value>
					</ows:AllowedValues>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>VORA</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Limit</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>In the raster mosaics this indicates that it is necessary to ignore an 'n' cells wide border of each of the original images</ows:Abstract>
				<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#integer">integer</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AnyValue/>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>RLE</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Compress and index IMG</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>When the output file is an IMG file, this file will be compressed and indexed.</ows:Abstract>
				<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#string">string</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AllowedValues>
						<ows:Value>##blank##</ows:Value>
					</ows:AllowedValues>
					<DefaultValue>##blank##</DefaultValue>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>LLINATGE</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Lineage</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>Pattern for the name of an additional raster file (actually one for each band) that indicates the source file index (starting from 0) that has contributed to each pixel of the output image. This file can help you understand the source of the data in each pixel of the output image.</ows:Abstract>
				<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#string">string</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AnyValue/>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>SIMPLIFICA_VERTEXS</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Simplify the intermediate vertices</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>Simplify the intermediate vertices of the arcs, as long as this does not mean a change in topology.</ows:Abstract>
				<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#string">string</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AllowedValues>
						<ows:Value>##blank##</ows:Value>
					</ows:AllowedValues>
					<DefaultValue>##blank##</DefaultValue>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>ALGORISME</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Algorithm</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract><![CDATA[This parameter is used to determine the type of algorithm that the application will use to cut the vectors in the topological structure.<ul><li> ESCOMBRATGE Based on the intersection of segments Bentley-Ottmann. </li><li>DIRECTE: Based on the exploration of all segments against all segments to determine the intersections between Victor by the topological structure.</li><li>AUTOMATIC: MiraMon automatically decides which of the two algorithms used.</li></ul>]]></ows:Abstract>
				<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#string">string</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AllowedValues>
						<ows:Value>ESCOMBRATGE</ows:Value>
						<ows:Value>DIRECTE</ows:Value>
						<ows:Value>AUTOMATIC</ows:Value>
					</ows:AllowedValues>
					<DefaultValue>AUTOMATIC</DefaultValue>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>TITOL</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Title</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>Output file title</ows:Abstract>
				<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#string">string</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AnyValue/>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>PATRO_DEST</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Pattern for result files</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>Common pattern for result files in case of multiband files.</ows:Abstract>
				<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#string">string</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AnyValue/>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>
		</DataInputs>
		<ProcessOutputs>
			<Output>
				<ows:Identifier>FitxerDesti</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Destination file</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>Is the name of the file resulting from the mosaic.</ows:Abstract>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Param2"/>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Name:DestinationFile"/>
				<ComplexOutput>
					<Default>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>application/x-img</MimeType>
							<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
						</Format>
					</Default>
					<Supported>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>application/x-img</MimeType>
							<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
						</Format>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>image/jpeg</MimeType>
							<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
						</Format>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>application/x-pnt</MimeType>
							<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
						</Format>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>application/x-pol</MimeType>
							<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
						</Format>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>application/x-arc</MimeType>
							<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
						</Format>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>application/x-nod</MimeType>
							<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
						</Format>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>image/png</MimeType>
							<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
						</Format>
					</Supported>
				</ComplexOutput>
			</Output>
		</ProcessOutputs>
	</ProcessDescription>
	<ProcessDescription wps:processVersion="1" storeSupported="true" statusSupported="false">
		<ows:Identifier>MiraMon:Mosaic:4</ows:Identifier>
		<ows:Title>Option 4</ows:Title>
		<ows:Abstract>The region to Mosaic is indicated by the extend of the EnvFile.</ows:Abstract>
		<DataInputs>
			<Input minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>Opcio</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Option</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>The region to Mosaic is indicated by the extend of the EnvFile.</ows:Abstract>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Param1"/>
				<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#integer">integer</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AllowedValues>
						<ows:Value>4</ows:Value>
					</ows:AllowedValues>
					<DefaultValue>4</DefaultValue>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>FitxerEnv</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Bounding box file</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>Is the file name where the extend will be extracted that will be used to cut the DestinationFile. Most of MiraMon formats are  suported.</ows:Abstract>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Param3"/>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Name:BBoxFile"/>
				<ComplexData>
					<Default>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>application/x-pol</MimeType>
							<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
						</Format>
					</Default>
					<Supported>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>application/x-pol</MimeType>
							<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
						</Format>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>application/x-nod</MimeType>
							<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
						</Format>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>application/x-arc</MimeType>
							<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
						</Format>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>application/x-pnt</MimeType>
							<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
						</Format>
					</Supported>
				</ComplexData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>FitxersFont</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Source files</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>Is a list of files written one after another in a command line or a text file that contains the names of the preexisting files to use.</ows:Abstract>
